6. Additional Concepts and Tips
Probability Distributions
Uniform Distribution: All outcomes are equally likely.
Binomial Distribution: Used when there are fixed numbers of independent trials, each with the same probability of success.
Normal Distribution: A continuous probability distribution useful for modeling many natural phenomena.
Handling Complex Events
When events involve combinations or complex conditions, consider using systematic enumeration or probability trees.
For overlapping events where the inclusion-exclusion principle applies, ensure that intersections are properly subtracted to avoid double counting.
Real-World Application
Risk Assessment: Calculating probabilities helps in determining the risk in various industries (finance, insurance).
Quality Control: In manufacturing, probability is used to model defects statistically.
Decision Making: Helps in making informed decisions under uncertainty.
